CORE libcxx
main.ii
--cpp11 --stdlib libc++ --unwind 6 --no-unwinding-assertions
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ size after fill ctor: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ content after fill ctor: SUCCESS$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
--
Representative of the round-129 libc++-23 sweep's persistent string
failure family: `std::string s(3, 'x')` against libc++-23 headers
(preprocessed in the cxx23-gate image; 17.5k lines).  Two pinned
diagnostics: `found no match for symbol '__rep'` (basic_string's
internal union rep accessor chain, __init_internal_buffer /
~basic_string) and `offset-of of member failed to find component
'__first_padding_' ` (datasizeof.h:44, _LIBCPP_DATASIZEOF machinery --
N5008 [basic.types.general] object-representation tail padding).  The
sweep (/tmp/docker_tumbleweed3.log, 2026-09-14) counts ~28 persistent
libc++-23 failures of which the string family is the largest block;
the vector family flipped CORE in round 128.
Round 163b (cvise reduction to 40 lines, /tmp/r163/red): the `__rep'
diagnostic was the functional cast `__rep()' of a union whose variant
member `__long' has a defaulted default constructor -- overload resolution
produced constructor candidates for struct types only, so
__init_internal_buffer and ~basic_string (both `__rep_ = __rep()') were
dropped and the string was nondet; and `__rep()' must zero-initialize
([dcl.init.general]/9.1).  Both fixed
(cpp11_union_value_initialization_defaulted_member,
cpp11_value_initialization_zero_initializes); the `__first_padding_byte_'
offsetof part was the member-class-template instantiation order, fixed
with cpp11_member_class_template_in_static_member_initializer.  The test
is CORE.  Still dropped: numeric_limits<>::max (<limits> line 202).
